Release Notes STM32MP15x OpenSTLinux BSP:
=========================================

BSP-Yocto-OpenSTLinux-STM32MP15x-PD25.1.0 2025-06-12
====================================================
- Linux ST Vendor Kernel v6.6.48
  * Tag v6.6-phy1
- U-boot ST Vendor v2023.10
  * Tag v2023.10-phy1
- TF-A ST Vendor v2.10
  * Tag v2.10-phy1
- OP-TEE ST Vendor 4.0.0
  * Tag 4.0.0-phy1
- Linux integration from STM32MP1-ecosystem-v6.0.2: "openstlinux-6.6-yocto-scarthgap-mpu-v25.03.19"
  (based on Yocto Scarthgap 5.0.3)

STM32CubeMP1 Package for Cortex-M4 development
----------------------------------------------
- v1.6.0-phy1: STM32CubeMP1 v1.6.0 + phyBOARD-Sargas board support
  https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu/wiki/STM32CubeMP1_Package_release_note_-_v1.6.0

Note:
This is still the same STM32CubeMP1 version as previous BSP PD23.1.1.
However a newer version "v1.7.0" bring by  STM32MP1-ecosystem-v6.0 could be used for newer developpment.
STM32CubeMP1 v1.7.0 release note: https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu/wiki/STM32CubeMP15_Package_release_note_-_v1.7.0

Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------
- st-image-weston (DISTRO=openstlinux-weston) on:
  * phycore-stm32mp1-3
  * phycore-stm32mp1-4

- st-image-weston (DISTRO=openstlinux-weston-rauc) on:
  * phycore-stm32mp1-3

- st-bundle-weston (DISTRO=openstlinux-weston-rauc) on:
  * phycore-stm32mp1-3

- st-image-core (DISTRO=openstlinux-weston) on:
  * phycore-stm32mp1-6

NOTES:
1) eglfs DISTRO is not supported anymore. But it can still be used if necessary as ST provides the distro file as sample in meta-st-openstlinux.
2) meta-qt5 is not part of the BSP anymore. The layer has to be added manually if needed (meta-qt5 or meta-qt6).

Build Environment:
------------------
- Ubuntu 20.04 64-bit

Fixes Issues:
-------------
- Fixes provided by OpenSTLinux v5.x and v6.0:
  For more details on those fixes, please refer to the following ST relase notes:
       * STM32MP1-ecosystem-v6.0: https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu/wiki/STM32_MPU_OpenSTLinux_release_note
       * OpenSTLinux v6.0: https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu/wiki/STM32_MPU_ecosystem_release_note

- Fixes provided by PHYTEC BSP adaptation:
    * Fix ONFI nand initialization:
       Some NAND device failed to boot (at TF-A boot stage) due to corrupted NAND parameter page.
       Add a fix to comply with the ONFI specification reading the redundant parameter page copies.

    * BSP build env initialization:
       The first created build directory name is now named "build" by default instead of "build-<DISTRO>-<MACHINE>".
       With the old name, the build could fails because file names exceed the maximum size supported
       by the file system (as Yocto is using absolute directory path to give names to intermediate files).

Features:
---------
- New features provided by OpenSTLinux v5.x and v6.0:
    For more details on those new features, please refer to the following ST relase notes:
       * STM32MP1-ecosystem-v6.0: https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu/wiki/STM32_MPU_OpenSTLinux_release_note
       * OpenSTLinux v6.0: https://wiki.st.com/stm32mpu/wiki/STM32_MPU_ecosystem_release_note

- New features provided by PHYTEC BSP adaptation:
     * OP-TEE is now activated by default. SP-MIN is not supported anymore.

- Existing features (from PD23.1.1 PHYTEC BSP release):
  * Boot support:
    * Boot from SD-card / eMMC / NAND / NOR-eMMC (Linux boot on eMMC)

  * Flash devices support:
    * eMMC (u-boot/kernel)
    * NAND (u-boot/kernel)
    * SPI NOR (u-boot/kernel)
    * SD-card (u-boot/kernel)

  * phyBOARD-Sargas addons support:
    * PEB-AV-01 support (HDMI module)
    * PEB-AV-02 with AC158 EDT 7" capacitive touch screen display support
    * MB1407 MIPI DSI screen support (4" touch screen display from STMicroelectronics)
    * PEB-WLBT-05 (2.4Ghz and 5Ghz version) support (WLAN/Bluetooth expansion)
    * phyCAM-P VM-016 BW & COL

  * Peripherals support:
    * I2C (u-boot/kernel)
    * UARTs (u-boot/kernel)
    * RS485 (kernel)
    * EEPROM (u-boot/kernel)
    * USB-Host (u-boot/kernel)
    * USB-OTG (u-boot/kernel)
    * Ethernet - 100Mpbs/1Gbps (u-boot/kernel)
    * CAN FD (kernel)
    * SPI (kernel)
    * Audio codec support (Line IN/OUT, Headphone) - TLV320AIC3007 (kernel)
    * RTC - RV-3028-C7 (kernel)
    * LED dimmer - PCA9533/01 (kernel)
    * User buttons support (kernel)
    * TIMERs (kernel)
    * ADCs (kernel)

  * Software Update support:
    RAUC support through our "openstlinux-weston-rauc" distribution (https://rauc.io/). Support is based on TF-A firmware update feature.

    Note: TF-A firmware update feature is not enabled by default. This feature is only enabled with our rauc distro.
    If necessary, it can be enabled without using rauc, just adding the following machine feature in the machine.conf file:
    MACHINE_FEATURES += "fw-update"

Known Issues/Limitations:
-------------------------
- Linux:
  * With "st-image-weston" and "phycore-stm32mp-x" yocto machines, following errors appears at the end of the boot on phyBOARD-Sargas:

    [ xxx ] st,stm32-sai-sub 4400a024.audio-controller: ASoC: error at snd_soc_dai_hw_params on 4400a024.audio-controller: -22
    [ xxx ] st,stm32-sai-sub 4400a024.audio-controller: Data size 32 larger than slot width

    Those errors appears several time when "wireplumber" is starting but sound is working correctly.
    On "st-image-core", there is no issue as "pipewire" and "wireplumber" are not part of the image (only ALSA).

- BSP build:
  * Following qualily checks warnings can appear at build time, but you can ignore them:
    "... uses 32-bit api ... Suppress with INSANE_SKIP ..."

- STM32CubeMP1 (Cortex-M4):
  * OpenAMP compilation issue with MDK-ARM when code generated through CubeMx:
    To avoid compiling errors in OpenAMP when compiling in MDK-ARM IDE, you have to disable the « Use MicroLIB » in « Target » tab.
